=== ws --help, piped
|ws — workspace manager CLI for DevPod environments with proxy support.
|
|Usage:
|  ws [command]
|
|Workspace Commands:
|  code     Open workspace in VS Code
|  delete   Delete a workspace
|  detect   Detect project profile
|  list     List workspaces
|  logs     Show workspace logs
|  new      Create a new workspace
|  restart  Restart a workspace
|  ssh      SSH into a workspace
|  start    Start a workspace
|  status   Show workspace health across all repositories
|  stop     Stop a workspace
|
|Profile Commands:
|  profile-create  Create a custom profile
|  profile-delete  Delete a custom profile
|  profiles        List available profiles
|
|Proxy Commands:
|  proxy  Proxy management commands
|
|Vault Commands:
|  vault  Vault-AI MCP operations
|
|Additional Commands:
|  completion  Generate shell completion script
|  help        Help about any command
|
|Flags:
|  -h, --help     help for ws
|      --json     Output in JSON format, where the command supports it
|  -v, --version  version for ws
|
|Use "ws [command] --help" for more information about a command.
=== ws proxy --help, piped
|Proxy management commands
|
|Usage:
|  ws proxy [command]
|
|Commands:
|  check           Verify proxy prerequisites
|  debug           Toggle debug logging
|  doctor          Run an ordered, fail-fast proxy diagnostic with remediation hints
|  down            Stop the proxy container
|  fix-routes      Fix default routes in workspace containers after reboot
|  init            Generate xray config from a VLESS or Hysteria2 URI
|  logs            Show proxy container logs
|  profile         Manage xray VLESS profiles
|  rebuild         Rebuild proxy image from scratch
|  recreate        Recreate the proxy container (destroys + creates new container)
|  restart         Restart the proxy container (preserves container, re-reads config)
|  status          Show proxy container status
|  test            Prove tunnel is active by comparing direct vs proxied exit IP
|  up              Start the proxy container
|  update          Update xray-core version
|  upgrade-config  Upgrade on-disk xray profiles to the current canonical inbound (adds sockopt.tproxy)
|
|Flags:
|  -h, --help  help for proxy
|
|Global Flags:
|      --json  Output in JSON format, where the command supports it
|
|Use "ws proxy [command] --help" for more information about a command.
=== ws proxy profile use --help, piped
|Validate, atomically swap, and reload the proxy so the new profile takes effect immediately.
|
|Use --no-reload to perform only the symlink swap (advanced — operator must run 'ws proxy restart' manually to apply).
|
|Usage:
|  ws proxy profile use <name> [flags]
|
|Flags:
|  -h, --help       help for use
|      --no-reload  Skip proxy restart after switching profile (advanced — operator must run 'ws proxy restart' manually to apply)
|
|Global Flags:
|      --json        Output in JSON format, where the command supports it
|      --no-migrate  Refuse auto-migration of legacy regular-file config.json; error out instead
=== ws list --help, piped
|List workspaces
|
|Usage:
|  ws list [flags]
|
|Aliases:
|  list, ls
|
|Flags:
|  -h, --help  help for list
|
|Global Flags:
|      --json  Output in JSON format, where the command supports it
=== ws vault doctor --help, piped
|Runs 5 read-only diagnostic checks per CONTEXT D-12: orphan MCP subprocesses, stale lock files, VAULT_AI_TOKEN presence, MCP fd-pass handshake, xrepo contract parity. Exit 0 (all green) / 1 (≥1 yellow) / 2 (≥1 red). Mutation is opt-in only via --kill-orphans + --clear-stale-locks (each gated by --yes or output.Confirm) per memory feedback_no_auto_state_mutation + Phase 22 D-09/D-10 lineage.
|
|Usage:
|  ws vault doctor [flags]
|
|Flags:
|      --clear-stale-locks  Remove stale lock files (opt-in mutation; gated by --yes / Confirm per CONTEXT D-13)
|  -h, --help               help for doctor
|      --kill-orphans       Kill detected orphan MCP subprocesses (opt-in mutation; gated by --yes / Confirm per CONTEXT D-13)
|      --yes                Skip confirmation prompts for --kill-orphans / --clear-stale-locks (Phase 22 D-09/D-10 discipline)
|
|Global Flags:
|      --json  Output in JSON format, where the command supports it
=== ws completion --help, piped
|Generate shell completion script for ws.
|
|# Zsh: add to ~/.zshrc
|eval "$(ws completion zsh)"
|
|# Bash: add to ~/.bashrc
|eval "$(ws completion bash)"
|
|# Fish: add to ~/.config/fish/config.fish
|ws completion fish | source
|
|Usage:
|  ws completion [bash|zsh|fish] [flags]
|
|Flags:
|  -h, --help  help for completion
|
|Global Flags:
|      --json  Output in JSON format, where the command supports it
